> ["p","q","r","s"]

"79"
> ["pw","px","py","pz","qw","qx","qy","qz","rw","rx","ry","rz","sw","sx","sy","sz"]

"234"
> ["adg","adh","adi","aeg","aeh","aei","afg","afh","afi","bdg","bdh","bdi","beg","beh","bei","bfg","bfh","bfi","cdg","cdh","cdi","ceg","ceh","cei","cfg","cfh","cfi"]

@@@ problem 77 combinations
title: Combinations
difficulty: Medium
topics: Backtracking
params: n, k
time: O(k · C(n, k))
space: O(k) extra (output excluded)
stress: 10
bench: n=10..20 step=+1 time=2^n space=2^n unit=n_(with_k_=_n/2)

=== description
Given integers `n` and `k`, return all possible combinations of `k` numbers chosen from `1..n`. The order of the combinations and of the numbers inside them does not matter (the judge sorts both).

=== constraints
- `1 <= n <= 20`
- `1 <= k <= n`

=== hints
- Choose numbers in increasing order to avoid duplicates: after picking `x`, only consider `x + 1 .. n`.
- Prune: if there aren't enough numbers left to reach `k`, stop early.

=== template
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> combine(int n, int k) {

    }
};

=== driver
LC_DRIVER {
    h.solve(&Solution::combine).sort_deep();
    h.gen([](lc::Gen &g, int n) {
        n = std::max(n, 1);
        return lc::lines(n, n >= 11 ? n / 2 : g.irange(1, n));
    });
}

=== approach
**Backtracking in increasing order.** `pick(start)` tries each number `x` from `start` upward, appends it, recurses with `start = x + 1`, then removes it. When the combination has `k` numbers, record it.

Pruning: if `cur` still needs `k - cur.size()` numbers, `x` can go at most up to `n - (k - cur.size()) + 1`; beyond that there aren't enough numbers left.

=== solution
class Solution {
    vector<vector<int>> out;
    vector<int> cur;

    void pick(int start, int n, int k) {
        if ((int)cur.size() == k) { out.push_back(cur); return; }
        int need = k - cur.size();
        for (int x = start; x <= n - need + 1; ++x) {   // leave room for the rest
            cur.push_back(x);
            pick(x + 1, n, k);
            cur.pop_back();
        }
    }

public:
    vector<vector<int>> combine(int n, int k) {
        out.clear();
        cur.clear();
        pick(1, n, k);
        return out;
    }
};

